    "result_text": "The suite is green. Done.\n\n## What I changed\n\n`membershipNumber` (formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of `registrationDate`'s year) is a server-derived, read-only field on the owner response. Three small edits, each low-impact:\n\n1. **New helper `MembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 mirrors the existing `HouseholdId` helper. A single static `of(customerCode, registrationDate)` computing `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, year % 100)`. Zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line delegating to the helper, exactly like the existing `householdId`/`displayName` mappings. The mapper method itself stays trivial.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `membershipNumber` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema (alongside `customerCode`/`householdId`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the property.\n\nThe derivation lives in its own cohesive unit rather than growing any existing method or class. `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass.",
